{
  "schemaVersion": "1.0.0",
  "id": "debug-double-render-pressure-v1",
  "family": "debug-double-render",
  "title": "Extra Renders Interview Pressure Mode",
  "access": "premium",
  "estimatedMinutes": 45,
  "supportedQuestions": {
    "react": "react-debug-double-render"
  },
  "rounds": [
    {
      "id": "one-click-one-render",
      "title": "One click, one render",
      "interviewerPrompt": "Every click currently renders the page twice. Find out why and fix the cause.",
      "constraints": [
        "Clicking `Increment` or `Reset` must add exactly 1 to the number in the element with the test id `renders`.",
        "Parity must always match the count: 0 is even, 1 is odd.",
        "Keep the starter test ids `count`, `parity` and `renders`."
      ],
      "frameworkTests": [
        {
          "id": "pressure-render-one-click",
          "name": "Round 1 · Each click renders once and parity stays right",
          "steps": [
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"renders\"]",
              "text": "1"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"count\"]",
              "text": "0"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"parity\"]",
              "text": "even"
            },
            {
              "type": "click",
              "selector": ".actions .btn",
              "index": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"count\"]",
              "text": "1"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"parity\"]",
              "text": "odd"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"renders\"]",
              "text": "2"
            },
            {
              "type": "click",
              "selector": ".actions .btn",
              "index": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"count\"]",
              "text": "2"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"parity\"]",
              "text": "even"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"renders\"]",
              "text": "3"
            },
            {
              "type": "click",
              "selector": ".actions .ghost",
              "index": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"count\"]",
              "text": "0"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"parity\"]",
              "text": "even"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"renders\"]",
              "text": "4"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "do-not-copy-props",
      "title": "Do not copy props into state",
      "interviewerPrompt": "The parity label is moving into its own component. It must not bring the same bug with it.",
      "constraints": [
        "Create a component named `ParityBadge` outside `App`. It receives `count` as a prop and shows the parity with the test id `parity`.",
        "Show how many times `ParityBadge` rendered, using the test id `badge-renders`. Count with `useRef`.",
        "One click must add exactly 1 to `badge-renders`. Do not copy the prop into state."
      ],
      "frameworkTests": [
        {
          "id": "pressure-render-badge",
          "name": "Round 2 · The badge renders once per click",
          "steps": [
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"badge-renders\"]",
              "text": "1"
            },
            {
              "type": "click",
              "selector": ".actions .btn",
              "index": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"parity\"]",
              "text": "odd"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"badge-renders\"]",
              "text": "2"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"renders\"]",
              "text": "2"
            },
            {
              "type": "click",
              "selector": ".actions .btn",
              "index": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"badge-renders\"]",
              "text": "3"
            },
            {
              "type": "click",
              "selector": ".actions .ghost",
              "index": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"parity\"]",
              "text": "even"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"badge-renders\"]",
              "text": "4"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "typing-leaves-the-badge-alone",
      "title": "Typing must not touch the badge",
      "interviewerPrompt": "Add a note field to the page. Typing a note has nothing to do with the badge, so the badge should not render at all.",
      "constraints": [
        "Add an input with the class `note-input` and show its text with the test id `note`.",
        "Wrap `ParityBadge` in `React.memo`. In this editor, write `React.memo`, not `memo`.",
        "Add a Reset button inside the badge with the class `badge-reset`. It receives its handler as a prop named `onReset` and sets the count to 0.",
        "Typing a note must add 0 to `badge-renders`, so `onReset` must keep the same identity between renders. Use `useCallback`."
      ],
      "frameworkTests": [
        {
          "id": "pressure-render-note",
          "name": "Round 3 · Typing a note leaves the badge alone",
          "steps": [
            {
              "type": "click",
              "selector": ".actions .btn",
              "index": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"renders\"]",
              "text": "2"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"badge-renders\"]",
              "text": "2"
            },
            {
              "type": "setValue",
              "selector": ".note-input",
              "value": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"note\"]",
              "text": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"renders\"]",
              "text": "3"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"badge-renders\"]",
              "text": "2"
            },
            {
              "type": "setValue",
              "selector": ".note-input",
              "value": "ab"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"note\"]",
              "text": "ab"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"renders\"]",
              "text": "4"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"badge-renders\"]",
              "text": "2"
            },
            {
              "type": "click",
              "selector": ".badge-reset"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"count\"]",
              "text": "0"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"badge-renders\"]",
              "text": "3"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"parity\"]",
              "text": "even"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "many-updates-one-render",
      "title": "Many updates, one render",
      "interviewerPrompt": "Two more reports came in: a button that loses updates, and a slow calculation that runs on every keystroke.",
      "constraints": [
        "Add a button with the class `add-five`. One click adds 1 five times, in five separate updates. The count goes up by 5 and renders by 1.",
        "Add a button with the class `add-later`. 200 ms after the click it adds 1 twice. The count goes up by 2 and renders by 1.",
        "Show the sum of 1 to `count` with the test id `sum`.",
        "Show how many times the sum was calculated with the test id `sum-runs`. It changes when the count changes, not when the note changes. Use `useMemo`."
      ],
      "frameworkTests": [
        {
          "id": "pressure-render-updates",
          "name": "Round 4 · Separate updates all count and render once",
          "steps": [
            {
              "type": "click",
              "selector": ".add-five"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"count\"]",
              "text": "5"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"renders\"]",
              "text": "2"
            },
            {
              "type": "click",
              "selector": ".add-later"
            },
            {
              "type": "wait",
              "durationMs": 300
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"count\"]",
              "text": "7"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"renders\"]",
              "text": "3"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "pressure-render-sum",
          "name": "Round 4 · The sum only recalculates when the count changes",
          "steps": [
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"sum\"]",
              "text": "0"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"sum-runs\"]",
              "text": "1"
            },
            {
              "type": "setValue",
              "selector": ".note-input",
              "value": "x"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"sum-runs\"]",
              "text": "1"
            },
            {
              "type": "click",
              "selector": ".actions .btn",
              "index": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"sum\"]",
              "text": "1"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"sum-runs\"]",
              "text": "2"
            },
            {
              "type": "setValue",
              "selector": ".note-input",
              "value": "xy"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"sum-runs\"]",
              "text": "2"
            },
            {
              "type": "click",
              "selector": ".add-five"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"sum\"]",
              "text": "21"
            },
            {
              "type": "expectText",
              "selector": "[data-testid=\"sum-runs\"]",
              "text": "3"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "debrief": {
    "title": "You removed every render that had no reason to happen",
    "summary": "You fixed the first bug at its cause, then kept finding the same family of problems: copied state, unstable props, lost updates and repeated work. The interview signal is explaining why a render happens before reaching for a tool that hides it.",
    "takeaways": [
      "A value that can be calculated from state should not be stored in state.",
      "Copying a prop into state brings the same extra render into a child component.",
      "`React.memo` only helps when the props keep their identity, which is why handlers need `useCallback`.",
      "Use a function update when the next value depends on the previous one."
    ],
    "frameworkNotes": {
      "react": "`StrictMode` can run renders twice in development, so measure in production or look for a state update as the real cause. Define components outside the parent, or they are rebuilt on every render."
    }
  },
  "solutionAssets": {
    "react": "assets/sb/react/solution/react-debug-double-render-pressure-solution.v1.json"
  }
}
